@startuml C4-Dynamic-ChatAiBff
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Dynamic — Explore Chat uses Explore AI through a BFF [planned]

autonumber
actor "End User" as user
participant "Chat Web / iOS" as client <<ui>>
participant "Chat API :9001\nAiController" as api <<java>>
participant "AiProxyService\n(ACL to Explore AI [planned])" as acl <<java>>
participant "Explore AI :9000\n/api (Published Language)" as ai <<java>>
participant "Ollama :11434" as ollama <<external>>

user -> client: Ask AI (text generate dialog)
client -> api: POST /api/v1/ai/chat\nAuthorization: Bearer (Chat or IAM token)

alt chat.upstreams.explore-ai configured [planned]
  api -> acl: Chat request (Chat terms)
  acl -> acl: Translate to Explore AI request,\npass the user's IAM token
  acl -> ai: POST /api/chat/... (Bearer)
  ai -> ai: JWT → owner, quota, module flags
  ai --> acl: Reply in Explore AI terms
  acl -> acl: Translate back to Chat terms
  acl --> api: Chat reply
else Today: explore-ai upstream empty
  api -> acl: chatOllama(body)
  acl -> ollama: POST /api/chat
  ollama --> acl: Model reply
  acl --> api: Reply map
end
api --> client: 200 reply\n502 Upstream unavailable on failure
client --> user: Show answer

note over api, ai
  Implemented today: AiController → AiProxyService → Ollama (chat) and Explore ML (media).
  Web /ai/explore/chat/stream is called by the client but has no Chat API handler yet.
  chat.upstreams.explore-ai exists but is blank; no Explore AI client is wired yet.
  Clients never call Explore AI directly; the BFF owns translation (ACL).
end note

@enduml
